    "description": "American Type 'Pacific' steam locomotive (4-6-2 wheel arrangement) in profile, drawn in the style of a 1930s shop drawing. A 2-axle pilot truck up front, three coupled drivers under the boiler, a single trailing axle under the firebox, and a 4-axle tender behind. Steam dome, sand dome, bell, headlight, brass boiler bands, side + main connecting rods, riveted plating. Stephenson's Rocket (1829) → Mallard (1938, 203 km/h world record).",
